{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And they called its name man.</b> Because it came in their mouths to say 'What is it? (man hu),' as we said above, it was called from that day forward 'man.' And they said it well, inadvertently — for man in place of mah (what) it is. And man is an expression of preparing food in Hebrew, as it is written: וימן להם המלך." "And it <b>was like coriander seed.</b> Because he said above 'fine as hoarfrost,' and hoarfrost has no fixed measure — sometimes coarse, sometimes fine — he went back and gave it a fixed measure by way of likeness: and the man was like coriander seed." "<b>Like seed.</b> The kaf with shva, and the zayin with segol." "<b>And its taste was like wafers in honey.</b> That they ate it as it was, but further on, when it says 'and they ground it in mills or beat it in a mortar,' its taste would change to the taste of creamy oil."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:18.428340931Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}